{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_011CfRyW8dBS4ujmudvsXChP","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01TvYhKorAALQG1P6wBj34s5","name":"StructuredOutput","input":{"tool_name":"final","arguments_json":"{\"response\":\"contract_version: 0.1.0\\nartifact_version: 1\\nwork_item: 20260908T113155\\nobservable_behaviour:\\n  - \\\"`evals/live.py` executes a genuinely isolated intent stage: when invoked with `--stage intent`, it runs only Stage 1 (`harness.intent.interpret_intent`, NL -> StructuredIntent) with no evidence fetch and no rendering, and grades it with a decision-scoped grader set only.\\\"\\n  - \\\"`evals/live.py` executes a genuinely isolated narration stage: when invoked with `--stage narration`, it builds an AnswerView via `harness.answer_view.build_answer_view` over a fixed/oracle envelope per case (NOT the model's own fetched envelope), calls `harness.narration.narrate`, and grades it with rendering/grounding/limitations graders only, so narration quality is scored independently of intent quality.\\\"\\n  - \\\"`--stage end-to-end` and `--stage` omitted continue to run the existing full trial (`ask(build_agent(), deps, phrasing)`) with the full grader set, unchanged except for the k=1 constraint already enforced for end-to-end.\\\"\\n  - \\\"The `stage` value now reaches execution and grading (threaded through `run_suite` -> `run_trial`), rather than only affecting report metadata and k/pressure validation as it does today.\\\"\\n  - \\\"A narration-stage trial fed a deliberately wrong scripted intent still passes/fails purely on the oracle envelope's rendering, proving isolation of narration from intent.\\\"\\n  - \\\"Quota-aware interruption, resumability and completed-trial aggregation are preserved for every stage: QuotaExceeded -> SuiteInterruption(kind=quota_exhausted) -> break; CredentialsRejected stops with no report; checkpoint-after-every-trial with atomic .tmp+.replace; --resume skips completed trials via _trial_key/done; pass@k and pass^k computed over completed trials only.\\\"\\nrequired_outputs:\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: evals/live.py\\n    reason: \\\"Thread `stage` into run_suite/run_trial and branch execution for intent-only, narration-only, and end-to-end trials while preserving quota/resume/checkpoint/accounting semantics.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: evals/graders.py\\n    reason: \\\"Add stage-scoped grader selection (INTENT_GRADERS, NARRATION_GRADERS from the existing decision/rendering partition) and a grade_case(case, record, stage=None) dispatch; stage=None preserves GRADERS_BY_DIRECTION exactly.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: evals/schema.py\\n    reason: \\\"Contingent minimal stage discriminator so an intent-only run (no rendered output) and a narration-only run (oracle envelope, no fetch) can be represented and attributed correctly. Modify only if isolation cannot be achieved without it.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: evals/replay.py\\n    reason: \\\"Contingent adjustment to project()/RunRecord construction so last_envelope()/evidence_calls() graders read the oracle envelope for narration and do not misfire on intent-only runs. Modify only if required.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_live_tier.py\\n    reason: \\\"Extend deterministic offline tests (scripted model) for per-stage execution, narration/intent isolation, per-stage checkpoint/resume, per-stage pass@k/pass^k, quota interruption, and CredentialsRejected-writes-no-report.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/live/test_live_eval.py\\n    reason: \\\"Add manual/credentialed coverage of the three-stage surface; remains live-marked and excluded from the PR gate.\\\"\\npermitted_files:\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: harness/intent.py\\n    reason: \\\"No logic change expected; a thin eval-facing helper may be added only if a stage cannot be invoked in isolation from the current signature (ADR-014 one-owner rule).\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: harness/narration.py\\n    reason: \\\"No logic change expected; a thin eval-facing helper may be added only if narration cannot be invoked in isolation. Production narration logic must not move into the eval runner.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: harness/answer_view.py\\n    reason: \\\"No logic change expected; reuse existing build_answer_view. A thin helper only if strictly required for oracle-envelope wiring.\\\"\\n  - repo: k-12Harness\\n    path: tests/unit/test_graders.py\\n    reason: \\\"ADR-013's meta-test test_every_grader_has_at_least_one_mutation scans the module's public graders and requires a load-bearing mutation for each. If the stage-scoped grading work adds any public grade_* grader, this enforcing file must gain the corresponding mutation(s); the graders-tests deterministic criterion runs it. It is permitted (not required) because the plan's declared changes do not name it and the edit is contingent on whether new public graders are introduced. The executor must satisfy this invariant, never implement around it by renaming graders private.\\\"\\ndeterministic:\\n  - id: full-test-suite\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/ -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The manifest verification command passes: the offline suite exits zero with no failures and no unexpected passes. Live-marked tests remain excluded from this gate (ADR-007).\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ failed'\\n  - id: contract-pin-unchanged\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The contract pin test still passes: no vendored contract file under contract/ changed and the registry version still equals settings.CONTRACT_VERSION (ADR-008).\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ failed'\\n  - id: live-tier-deterministic-tests\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_live_tier.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The deterministic (scripted-model) live-tier tests pass, covering per-stage execution and grading, narration/intent isolation, per-stage checkpoint/resume without repeating completed trials, per-stage pass@k/pass^k over completed trials only, quota interruption leaving a resumable checkpoint, and CredentialsRejected writing no report.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ failed'\\n  - id: graders-tests\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/unit/test_graders.py -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"The adversarial grader tests still pass: existing graders' pass/fail rules are unchanged and every grader still carries a load-bearing mutation (ADR-013). Stage-scoped selection does not weaken any grader, and any new public grade_* grader carries its own mutation.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\n      stdout_excludes: '\\\\d+ failed'\\n  - id: live-eval-collect-only\\n    repo: k-12Harness\\n    command: \\\".venv/bin/python -m pytest tests/live/test_live_eval.py --collect-only -m live -q\\\"\\n    expected: \\\"Selecting the live marker explicitly collects the new three-stage manual coverage: the file collects cleanly under `-m live` and exits zero (at least one live test is selected), proving the live-marked tests are present and, since the repository's default addopts `-m 'not live'` deselects them, that they stay excluded from the default PR gate (ADR-007). Marker completeness of the file is additionally proven by the unit assertion inside the full-test-suite gate.\\\"\\n    expect:\\n      exit_code: 0\\nmust_not_change:\\n  - \\\"Any vendored contract file under contract/ (registry, schemas, PINNED.json); the v0.3.0 evidence contract is out of scope and pinned by hash (ADR-008).\\\"\\n  - \\\"tests/unit/test_contract_pin.py and the contract pin it enforces.\\\"\\n  - \\\"The pass/fail rule of any existing grader in evals/graders.py; only stage-scoped selection may be added (ADR-013).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Production decision, fetch, rendering-gate, and assembly logic in harness/agent.py, harness/rendering.py, harness/outputs.py; the eval runner must not duplicate or reimplement stage-owner logic (ADR-014).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Credential/transport semantics: CredentialsRejected stops the suite with no report; a 500/timeout remains an ordinary failed trial; classification stays status-based via classify (ADR-016).\\\"\\n  - \\\"cost_complete semantics: it requires that something was actually priced, and remains False by design under the claude_account transport (ADR-016, ADR-019).\\\"\\n  - \\\"The _trial_key = (case_id, phrasing, trial) definition and the checkpoint stage-guard that forbids resuming across a different stage.\\\"\\n  - \\\"The deterministic stub-tier pass/fail rules and golden-case authoring format (beyond any per-stage oracle wiring narration requires).\\\"\\nfailure_behaviour:\\n  - \\\"On QuotaExceeded during any stage, the runner raises/records SuiteInterruption(kind=quota_exhausted, reset_at=...) and breaks, leaving a resumable checkpoint written atomically after the last completed trial.\\\"\\n  - \\\"On a rejected credential in any stage, run_trial surfaces CredentialsRejected (via classify -> AuthError), main stops at the first occurrence, and no report is written (ADR-016).\\\"\\n  - \\\"A 500, timeout, or other ordinary error in any stage is recorded as a failed TrialResult, not folded into an infrastructure stop and not scored as a credential/auth failure (ADR-016).\\\"\\n  - \\\"An intent-only trial performs no evidence fetch and no rendering; a narration-only trial performs no live fetch and narrates over the oracle envelope only. A stage that cannot be executed in isolation must fail loudly rather than silently falling back to the full end-to-end path.\\\"\\n  - \\\"A resume whose recorded stage differs from the requested stage remains rejected rather than silently mixing cross-stage trials.\\\"\\ncompatibility:\\n  - \\\"Live tier stays manual/nightly and never becomes a PR gate; it reports pass@k (capability) and pass^k (reliability) separately for each stage (ADR-007, ADR-015).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Grading reads the transcript / the envelope the tool actually returned (for narration, the oracle envelope), never the model's account of its own work (ADR-013).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Limitations render verbatim and the harness assigns no grade; narration and end-to-end grading must continue to enforce this (ADR-009).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Default (--stage omitted) and end-to-end both keep the current full-loop execution; their only difference remains the k=1 constraint already enforced for end-to-end.\\\"\\n  - \\\"Account-plan (claude_account) usage is reported without a manufactured USD figure; cost_complete remains False there, and spend_usd(deps.last_messages) still applies where a model call occurred (ADR-018, ADR-019).\\\"\\ncompatibility_baselines: []\\ncontract_requirements:\\n  - \\\"The manifest declares no explicit allowlist for k-12Harness (governance diff-allowlist, scope.declared_files: [], declared: false). The permitted change set is exactly the files in required_outputs plus permitted_files; a change exceeding this set is a scope escape requiring human review, not silent expansion.\\\"\\n  - \\\"SCOPE (recontract v4): tests/unit/test_graders.py is added to permitted_files. Contract v3 permitted evals/graders.py but not its enforcing test; ADR-013's test_every_grader_has_at_least_one_mutation requires a mutation for every public grader, so a stage-scoped grading change that introduces public grade_* graders cannot pass v3's scope. Attempt 7 escaped the invariant by renaming graders private; that is not acceptable. The executor must add the required mutation(s) within scope.\\\"\\n  - \\\"CONFLICT (request vs current source): request.md assumes the three stages are executed, but evals/live.py today ships an inert --stage surface (parsed, validated, checkpointed, resume-guarded) whose value never reaches run_suite/run_trial/grading. The work is to wire the existing flag into execution and grading, NOT to add a new flag.\\\"\\n  - \\\"GAP (no defining authority): 'genuinely isolated' stage semantics, oracle-narration input, and per-stage grader sets have no schema/ADR that specifies them exactly. They are interpreted from the request plus ADR-013's transcript/envelope isolation principle and the existing four-stage pipeline; this interpretation is a proposal for human confirmation.\\\"\\n  - \\\"ASSUMPTION (load-bearing, needs owner confirmation): 'isolated narration' means grading against a canonical/oracle envelope per case (the existing case.stub_case fixture) built into an AnswerView, not the model's own fetched envelope. If isolation instead means isolating narration from intent while still performing a live fetch, the wiring differs and the contract must be revised.\\\"\\n  - \\\"GAP (no defining source for operational guarantees): request.md requires 'quota-aware checkpointing, resumability, completed-trial semantics' but docs/decisions.md ADR-016 defines only credential/transport-failure handling; quota-exhaustion signalling and checkpoint format are otherwise undefined and are preserved from current source behaviour as-is.\\\"\\n  - \\\"GAP (provider authority ambiguous): ADR-018 (codex_account) and ADR-019 (claude_account, superseding) both appear in the pack; the governing quota transport is taken to be claude_account per ADR-019, but the exact QuotaExceeded raise site is unconfirmed from available source.\\\"\\n  - \\\"CONSTRAINT (RunRecord shape): evals/schema.RunRecord / evals/replay.project cannot currently represent an intent-only run (no rendered output) or a narration-only run (oracle envelope, no fetch). Any change here must be the smallest that lets existing graders read the oracle envelope for narration and prevents last_envelope()/evidence_calls() misattribution; it must not alter end-to-end RunRecord shape or grading.\\\"\\nsemantic:\\n  - \\\"Isolation (the defining check): a narration-stage trial given a wrong scripted intent scores identically to one given a correct intent, because grounding, limitations_verbatim, confidence_unchanged, and no_forecast_framing all read the oracle envelope, not the intent.\\\"\\n  - \\\"An intent-stage trial is graded only by decision-scoped graders (question_match, request_match, school_resolved_through_directory, clarification_correct, refusal_is_contract_sourced); rendering/grounding graders do not run and no evidence is fetched.\\\"\\n  - \\\"grade_case(..., stage=None) reproduces the current GRADERS_BY_DIRECTION behaviour exactly for end-to-end/default trials, so existing reference solutions and mutations remain load-bearing (ADR-013).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Per-stage completed-trial accounting: summarise/aggregate/completed_reports count each completed stage-scoped trial exactly once and match a hand-computed trial matrix per stage; pass@k/pass^k are reported separately per stage.\\\"\\n  - \\\"The eval runner reuses the harness's public stage entry points (interpret_intent, build_answer_view, narrate) rather than duplicating decision or render logic (ADR-014).\\\"\\nout_of_scope:\\n  - \\\"Changing the v0.3.0 evidence contract, registry, schemas, or PINNED.json (pinned; adoption of a new contract version is a separate deliberate change).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Production agent decision logic and the four-stage pipeline in harness/agent.py beyond exposing existing entry points for isolated invocation.\\\"\\n  - \\\"The deterministic stub-tier pass/fail rules and the golden-case authoring format, except any per-stage oracle-envelope wiring narration requires.\\\"\\n  - \\\"Adding or redesigning the --stage CLI surface (parsing/validation/checkpoint/resume-guard already exist); the work is wiring the existing value into execution and grading.\\\"\\n  - \\\"Wiring the FastAPI server layer (server/), the demo surface, and any change to live-tier scheduling (it stays manual, never a PR gate).\\\"\\n  - \\\"Altering _trial_key composition or introducing cross-stage trial mixing on resume.\\\"\\n\"}"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":129381,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":129381},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"2fa6a52d-dcbc-4ba7-963e-74be7fd4df06","uuid":"3b9cae49-0ae4-4f7d-9ce8-3067471c0f6c","request_id":"req_011CfRyW7dQ3aZoM2vAj1pUX"}
